WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.222 --> 00:00:04.262
This video is brought to you by Henson Shaving.

00:00:04.262 --> 00:00:08.342
Tesla has fascinated the world with&nbsp;
its cool and fast electric cars.

00:00:08.342 --> 00:00:12.182
Now it wants to disrupt a&nbsp;
related industry: insurance.

00:00:12.182 --> 00:00:15.702
Tesla has been quietly selling car&nbsp;
insurance for the last couple of years.

00:00:15.702 --> 00:00:18.022
But it won’t be quiet for much longer.

00:00:18.022 --> 00:00:23.622
CEO Elon Musk believes insurance will one&nbsp;
day account for a third of Tesla’s business.

00:00:23.622 --> 00:00:25.862
It will be much more compelling&nbsp;
than anything else out there.

00:00:25.862 --> 00:00:28.822
It’s gonna cost less and be&nbsp;
better, so, why wouldn’t you?

00:00:28.822 --> 00:00:33.222
Tesla started selling personal car&nbsp;
insurance in California in 2019&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.222 --> 00:00:38.582
and claims drivers can trim their insurance&nbsp;
costs by as much as 20% or 30%.

00:00:38.582 --> 00:00:42.822
Data compiled by the personal financial&nbsp;
website ValuePenguin shows Tesla Insurance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.822 --> 00:00:47.222
is not the cheapest in California but&nbsp;
it is amongst the least expensive.

00:00:47.222 --> 00:00:51.622
It is said to be the least costly plan&nbsp;
in Texas where Tesla has a lot going on.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.622 --> 00:00:55.142
A new Gigafactory is being built&nbsp;
near Austin. And Musk permanently&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.142 --> 00:00:59.782
moved to the Lonestar state to be closer&nbsp;
to SpaceX’s rocket facility for Starship.

00:00:59.782 --> 00:01:04.342
State regulators there have reportedly approved&nbsp;
the rates and policies for Tesla Insurance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.342 --> 00:01:10.022
which, according to data compiled by&nbsp;
ValuePenguin, is $1,795 on average.

00:01:10.022 --> 00:01:13.382
Individual rates do differ greatly&nbsp;
depending on your driving record,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.382 --> 00:01:16.582
age, how much coverage you&nbsp;
choose, and the Tesla you buy.

00:01:16.582 --> 00:01:20.422
The Model Y mid-size SUV is&nbsp;
the least expensive to insure.

00:01:20.422 --> 00:01:23.702
And if you take the Model S, rates&nbsp;
could be more expensive for the Plaid,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.702 --> 00:01:29.782
which goes 0 to 100 in 2.1 seconds compared&nbsp;
with the long-range version’s 3.2 seconds.

00:01:29.782 --> 00:01:32.982
So, why can Tesla afford to&nbsp;
offer lower insurance rates?

00:01:32.982 --> 00:01:36.742
It says it will do away with fees taken&nbsp;
by traditional insurance carriers.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.742 --> 00:01:40.182
An example of fees is commissions&nbsp;
paid to insurance brokers.

00:01:40.182 --> 00:01:45.142
And more importantly - Tesla argues no&nbsp;
one knows more about a Tesla than Tesla.

00:01:45.142 --> 00:01:48.022
While other insurance companies&nbsp;
set their insurance rates based on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.022 --> 00:01:53.142
their own risk assessments, which could be&nbsp;
inflated because the technology is so new,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.142 --> 00:01:57.942
Tesla believes only it knows the cars&nbsp;
well enough to determine fair rates.

00:01:57.942 --> 00:02:02.182
The insane amount of data collected&nbsp;
from its cars tracks how fast you drive,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.182 --> 00:02:04.902
the number of times the lane&nbsp;
departure warning is triggered,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.902 --> 00:02:08.342
whether you’re in ludicrous mode&nbsp;
or the even faster plaid mode.

00:02:08.342 --> 00:02:13.062
Although Tesla says it does share driving data&nbsp;
with other insurers - the belief is that it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.062 --> 00:02:17.942
“...uniquely understands its vehicles,&nbsp;
technology, safety, and repair costs.”

00:02:17.942 --> 00:02:22.822
For the moment, Tesla says it doesn’t use your&nbsp;
personal driving data to determine insurance rates&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.822 --> 00:02:26.742
but that will almost certainly change&nbsp;
in the future. Musk has hinted at this.

00:02:26.742 --> 00:02:30.502
If they want to buy Tesla insurance,&nbsp;
they have to agree to not drive the car&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.502 --> 00:02:33.702
in a crazy way. Or, they can, but&nbsp;
then the insurance rates higher.

00:02:33.702 --> 00:02:37.142
Toyota has already been testing this&nbsp;
out. It partnered with insurance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.142 --> 00:02:40.022
company Progressive to start&nbsp;
tracking driving behaviors in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.022 --> 00:02:43.782
Toyotas with connected technology&nbsp;
to potentially offer discounts.

00:02:43.782 --> 00:02:47.542
There’s a lot of room for discounting&nbsp;
when it comes to electric vehicles.

00:02:47.542 --> 00:02:51.862
The typical insurance company has&nbsp;
been found to price EVs at 23%&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.862 --> 00:02:56.982
more than a gas-powered equivalent primarily&nbsp;
due to the expensive cost of repairing them.

00:02:56.982 --> 00:03:02.022
A few years ago, a writer for CleanTechnica&nbsp;
described clipping a parking sign in his Model 3&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.022 --> 00:03:05.222
and the repair bill was nearly a whopping $7,000.

00:03:05.222 --> 00:03:07.622
A big chunk of that was labor costs&nbsp;
because of the technology in the car:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.622 --> 00:03:11.862
the sensors needed to be recalibrated&nbsp;
and the battery connectors disconnected.

00:03:11.862 --> 00:03:15.222
Tesla thinks it has an advantage&nbsp;
here as well. The company says its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.222 --> 00:03:19.542
own service centers can work four&nbsp;
times faster than conventional ones.

00:03:19.542 --> 00:03:23.142
The number of Tesla repair centers&nbsp;
has been rapidly expanding.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.142 --> 00:03:27.916
And the goal is to reportedly open up
one new shop every week in 2021.

00:03:28.022 --> 00:03:30.262
But ultimately, Tesla wants to make its vehicles&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.262 --> 00:03:33.862
so reliable that you won’t really&nbsp;
need to visit a service center.

00:03:33.862 --> 00:03:37.382
Tesla believes its self-driving&nbsp;
software called Full Self-Driving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.382 --> 00:03:41.222
or FSD will make its cars safer&nbsp;
and less prone to accidents.

00:03:41.222 --> 00:03:44.182
This is the software that Tesla&nbsp;
hopes will take its cars from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.182 --> 00:03:47.782
Level 2 autonomy in which the driver&nbsp;
has to be prepared to take the wheel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.782 --> 00:03:52.502
all the way up to Level 5 in which the driver&nbsp;
doesn’t have to pay any attention at all.

00:03:52.502 --> 00:03:57.062
Tesla will even offer insurance discounts for&nbsp;
those using their driver assistance systems.

00:03:57.062 --> 00:03:59.942
If and when Teslas are able&nbsp;
to fully drive themselves,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.942 --> 00:04:05.302
it doesn’t mean accidents won’t happen. Technology&nbsp;
can fail or humans can fail to use it properly.

00:04:05.302 --> 00:04:08.662
So how on earth will other&nbsp;
insurance companies assess the risk?

00:04:08.662 --> 00:04:12.262
It will be easier over time as more&nbsp;
data comes in that will better inform&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.262 --> 00:04:15.222
companies about pricing risk in line with reality.

00:04:15.222 --> 00:04:19.302
But they may have a hard time catching up to&nbsp;
Tesla, which is now seeking to offer coverage&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.302 --> 00:04:25.462
in Texas, Illinois, and Washington. The goal is&nbsp;
nationwide coverage, and one day, perhaps, global.

00:04:25.462 --> 00:04:29.222
It’s clear that Tesla wants to offer&nbsp;
a complete package to the consumer.

00:04:29.222 --> 00:04:33.542
Apple has done this successfully by creating&nbsp;
an ecosystem where its devices are designed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.542 --> 00:04:37.302
to work seamlessly with one another&nbsp;
which entices you to buy them all.

00:04:37.302 --> 00:04:42.342
Tesla is now trying to build its own ecosystem in&nbsp;
which your house has a Tesla solar roof that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.342 --> 00:04:46.982
generates energy that can be stored in a Tesla&nbsp;
powerwall which can power your home at night or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.982 --> 00:04:51.862
during an outage. The powerwall can also charge&nbsp;
your Tesla, then you can purchase Autopilot and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.862 --> 00:04:57.942
full self-driving software for your car, and your&nbsp;
car is conveniently covered by Tesla Insurance.

00:04:57.942 --> 00:05:00.502
But not everyone is a fan of the insurance plan.

00:05:00.502 --> 00:05:05.542
Berkshire Hathaway CEO Warren Buffett said&nbsp;
bluntly at an annual shareholders meeting that:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.542 --> 00:05:09.542
“The success of the auto companies getting&nbsp;
into the insurance business is probably&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.542 --> 00:05:13.862
as likely as the success of the insurance&nbsp;
companies getting into the auto business.”

00:05:13.862 --> 00:05:18.422
Buffett became one of the wealthiest people&nbsp;
on earth by investing in insurance companies.

00:05:18.422 --> 00:05:23.382
Despite his skepticism, Musk has proven&nbsp;
his doubters wrong time and time again.

00:05:23.382 --> 00:05:27.222
He believes Tesla Insurance&nbsp;
will be stunningly successful.

00:05:27.222 --> 00:05:32.022
Insurance could very well be, I don’t know, 30%,&nbsp;
40% of the value of the car business, frankly.

00:05:32.022 --> 00:05:37.462
If Tesla reaches its goal of producing 20 million&nbsp;
cars a year by 2030, and you multiply that by

00:05:37.462 --> 00:05:44.102
$1,795 in annual insurance&nbsp;
premiums - that brings in $36 billion a year.

00:05:44.102 --> 00:05:47.382
That’s $36 billion year after year after year!

00:05:47.382 --> 00:05:51.142
And owners of a robotaxi - the planned&nbsp;
ride sharing network - would likely pay&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.142 --> 00:05:55.302
higher premiums due to the many more&nbsp;
hours the vehicles are on the road.

00:05:55.302 --> 00:05:58.662
In the way that Tesla has been&nbsp;
revolutionizing the car industry,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.662 --> 00:06:02.182
Musk is betting it can do the same&nbsp;
to the car insurance business.

00:06:02.742 --> 00:06:07.222
There’s also another company revolutionizing&nbsp;
an industry: the shaving industry!

00:06:07.222 --> 00:06:11.302
When Henson Shaving reached out about trying&nbsp;
their razor and possibly sponsoring a video,&nbsp;&nbsp;

